'The same reasoning applies to gaze, pointing and personal space. A child who looks down may still demonstrate accurate understanding. Asking whether a seating arrangement is comfortable provides individual evidence. Food and religious examples in the slides are topics for contextual inquiry, not verified rulings about every community or individual. A religious-legal determination would require appropriate sources and is not established by a sociolinguistic example.'
